    "title": "Oklahoma QB John Mateer Questionable vs. Texas - Injury Update",
    "text": "Oklahoma quarterback John Mateer is‌ officially listed as questionable for Saturday’s Red River⁢ Rivalry ⁢game ⁢against Texas,according to the initial SEC availability report released Wednesday. The potential absence of the Heisman Trophy ‍contender throws uncertainty into the highly anticipated matchup between the No. 6 Sooners and the⁤ Longhorns.\nMateer is recovering from hand surgery‍ performed on Sept. 24, but has been ‌pushing for an earlier-than-expected ⁢return, ​sources ‍told ESPN’s Pete Thamel. Oklahoma coach ​Brent Venables deferred questions about Mateer’s status ⁢to the availability report, stating, “It’ll come out here tonight and everybody ​will get it at the same time.”\nThe injury occurred during Oklahoma’s 24-17 victory over Auburn on Sept. 20, where Mateer completed 24 of 36 passes for 271 yards ​despite being injured in the first quarter. He has missed only one game since‌ the surgery, with ‌the Sooners utilizing a bye week and a 44-0 win ‍over Kent State.‍\nduring the Kent State game, Michael Hawkins Jr.started at quarterback and ⁣led Oklahoma ⁢to victory.Further availability reports will be released ⁣Thursday and Friday evenings, with a final report issued 90 minutes before the 3:30 p.m.‌ ET kickoff in Dallas.\nESPN’s Eli Lederman ⁢contributed to this report.",
